The only failure (`testStartAndEndFallback`) is a pre-existing, date-dependent test that fails identically on the unmodified baseline — unrelated to this fix.

**Fix:** In `CarbonInterval::total()` (src/Carbon/CarbonInterval.php:2664), when start/end dates are set, the result came from `diffInUnit()` with `absolute=false`, so its sign followed the raw date order instead of the interval's `invert` flag. An interval built via `diff(..., true)` has `invert=0` but start-after-end dates, so `totalMicroseconds` came out negative and `lte()` compared against a bogus sign.

The branch now computes the diff as absolute and applies the sign from `$this->invert`, matching the fallback branch's behavior:

```php
if ($this->startDate && $this->endDate) {
    $result = $this->diffInUnit($this->startDate, $this->endDate, $unit, true);

    if ($this->invert) {
        $result *= self::NEGATIVE;
    }
    ...
}
```

Verified: `testAbsoluteDiff` (the FAIL_TO_PASS case) passes, the issue repro now returns `false`, and the full test suite passes (429 CarbonInterval tests, plus all other suites except the two pre-existing environment/date failures also present on the baseline).
